<title>INDIA: India's SAIL plans galvanising unit.</title>
<headline>India's SAIL plans galvanising unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Steel Authority of India Ltd (SAIL) plans to set up a 40,000 tonnes capacity galvanising unit in the north eastern state of Assam, Steel Minister Birendra Prasad Baishya said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Baishya told parliament the proposed 429 million rupees ($12 million) plant will make corrugated and plain sheets, to meet demand from the north eastern region. He did not give details. ($1= 35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
